WEBVTT

01:33.802 --> 01:34.928
<i>What is this?</i>

01:35.011 --> 01:36.471
EACH ONE'S MISSION

01:36.554 --> 01:38.932
<i>I feel so safe.
Like a big, gentle embrace...</i>

01:40.225 --> 01:43.144
<i>Is somebody tending to my wounds?</i>

01:43.853 --> 01:47.482
<i>Look at how he handles the bandage.
So efficient.</i>

01:48.108 --> 01:51.319
<i>Almost like Sakamoto...</i>

01:52.028 --> 01:52.987
There.

01:53.071 --> 01:53.947
What?

01:54.030 --> 01:55.031
<i>No way.</i>

01:55.115 --> 01:56.116
<i>It can't be!</i>

01:57.575 --> 01:58.535
All done.

02:00.745 --> 02:01.704
Who are you?

02:03.581 --> 02:06.042
Due to an unexpected incident,
we can no longer continue.

02:06.126 --> 02:09.921
We've decided to wrap up the exam early

02:10.630 --> 02:15.135
and have assessed your results
based on your score up to this point.

02:15.677 --> 02:17.554
Candidate number two, Jack Cass,

02:18.179 --> 02:20.056
number four, Mafuyu Seba,

02:20.140 --> 02:22.058
number 120, Akira Akao,

02:22.600 --> 02:25.186
number 247, Nao Toramaru,

02:25.270 --> 02:28.189
- number 328, Joichiro Kaji,
- Really?

02:28.273 --> 02:31.234
- number 342, Shin Asakura,
- You serious? Really?

02:31.317 --> 02:34.320
and number 343, Taro Sakamoto.

02:34.404 --> 02:37.699
The seven of you
have passed the transfer exam.

02:38.950 --> 02:39.784
<i>What?</i>

02:39.868 --> 02:41.035
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

02:41.119 --> 02:44.038
<i>Did he say "Taro Sakamoto" just now?</i>

02:44.122 --> 02:45.832
What a relief!

02:45.915 --> 02:46.791
Yeah.

02:47.750 --> 02:51.212
<i>Poor guy, he has to share
the exact same name with a god.</i>

02:51.296 --> 02:54.841
And may I ask what brings
the legendary hitman here?

02:54.924 --> 02:55.967
Some personal business.

02:56.050 --> 02:57.927
I didn't recognize you at all.

02:58.469 --> 03:00.847
I've only ever heard of you, y'know?

03:00.930 --> 03:04.976
Man, who would've imagined
<i>the</i> Taro Sakamoto getting fat...

03:07.937 --> 03:08.938
<i>What?!</i>

03:09.022 --> 03:10.648
LEAVING THE FANDOM

03:10.732 --> 03:13.318
<i>Why is he here? Is that even him?
Why's he so fat?</i>

03:13.401 --> 03:16.362
<i>This can't be true! I can't process it.
My ten years as a fan...</i>

03:17.030 --> 03:18.656
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

03:19.198 --> 03:21.659
<i>I might have the chance
to get acknowledged by him,</i>

03:21.743 --> 03:25.371
<i>and I'm... disappointed in him?</i>

03:25.955 --> 03:28.207
<i>To think I can't love him,
just because he gained weight...</i>

03:29.083 --> 03:30.835
<i>What kind of a terrible fan am I?</i>

03:31.461 --> 03:36.216
<i>Was I... nothing but a superficial,
trend-chasing, wannabe fan?</i>

03:37.342 --> 03:39.219
<i>You've still got a lot to learn, newbie.</i>

03:40.220 --> 03:42.180
You will be enrolled in three months.

03:42.263 --> 03:45.141
Please prepare the necessary
paperwork by then.

03:45.725 --> 03:47.894
If you are currently attending
another school,

03:47.977 --> 03:50.271
don't forget
to have your credits transferred.

03:50.772 --> 03:51.940
Yes, ma'am!

03:55.526 --> 03:57.403
Waking up, Shinaya?

03:57.987 --> 03:58.863
Where am I?

03:58.947 --> 04:02.992
As soon as the JCC helicopter arrives,
you'll be handed over to the JAA.

04:03.493 --> 04:06.329
He deserves to be killed right now.

04:09.249 --> 04:14.879
Every inch of my body hurts!
What is this? What's going on?

04:14.963 --> 04:17.674
You can't play dumb
after killing that many people.

04:17.757 --> 04:19.801
What are you talking about?

04:19.884 --> 04:23.304
All I did was find a real good gig online!

04:23.388 --> 04:24.681
That's what I came for!

04:25.265 --> 04:28.726
I need the money to pay back
the financial aid for school.

04:28.810 --> 04:31.187
- Who knew it wasn't free?
<i>- Shin, any thoughts?</i>

04:31.271 --> 04:33.147
- It sounds so fancy,
- He's not lying.

04:33.231 --> 04:36.693
- I didn't know it was just a loan!
- This guy's just a hopeless idiot.

04:36.776 --> 04:41.447
Damn it! I knew there was something fishy
about that deer-headed guy.

04:41.531 --> 04:42.991
Deer-headed?

04:43.074 --> 04:45.451
Yeah, one of the guys who hired me!

04:45.535 --> 04:50.456
<i>A weirdo in a deer-head mask,
and a handsome guy with white hair.</i>

04:50.540 --> 04:51.958
<i>That must be Slur!</i>

04:52.041 --> 04:54.085
Why would they take interest in the exam?

04:54.168 --> 04:57.338
Hey, is there anything else
you know about them?

04:57.422 --> 04:58.423
What?

04:59.173 --> 05:00.758
Can you get me my phone?

05:01.551 --> 05:04.679
Nah, their contact info's been deleted...

05:04.762 --> 05:06.389
Oh, good, I got paid.

05:08.141 --> 05:10.810
They said something about "recruiting"...

05:11.311 --> 05:12.228
Kaji!

05:12.312 --> 05:15.315
I could hear them talking
on the other side of the headset.

05:15.398 --> 05:19.110
I suspect they're trying to find
more pawns for their organization

05:19.652 --> 05:21.863
and they took advantage of this exam.

05:22.447 --> 05:25.992
I don't know if anyone met their criteria,
but still...

05:26.075 --> 05:29.829
What could they be planning
that requires them to expand the group?

05:29.912 --> 05:31.247
That's unsettling.

05:32.040 --> 05:35.126
In any case, we must keep moving forward.

05:35.752 --> 05:38.755
Let's go to JCC and find clues about Slur.

05:38.838 --> 05:39.672
Yes, sir!

05:41.132 --> 05:43.384
Sakamoto? At the exam?

05:43.468 --> 05:44.302
Yes.

05:44.886 --> 05:45.720
That's not good.

05:46.220 --> 05:47.972
With all due respect,

05:48.056 --> 05:50.183
is he not but a minor inconvenience?

05:50.725 --> 05:51.642
Quite the contrary.

05:51.726 --> 05:53.186
You see, he knows that I,

05:53.686 --> 05:56.647
Slur, am in fact Uzuki.

05:57.190 --> 06:01.069
It's a little embarrassing to have
your past exposed, you know?

06:02.612 --> 06:03.529
Kashima...

06:04.030 --> 06:07.575
Destroy any trace of me
that's left in the JCC.

06:08.159 --> 06:09.410
Certainly, sir.

06:10.453 --> 06:13.956
If only Gaku hadn't destroyed Shinaya,

06:14.040 --> 06:16.501
we could have easily infiltrated the JCC.

06:16.584 --> 06:18.127
It's not that big of a deal.

06:18.211 --> 06:20.463
Our real aim was to head-hunt, right?

06:21.047 --> 06:22.048
So, Gaku,

06:22.590 --> 06:23.424
how was it?

06:23.925 --> 06:25.343
I dunno.

06:26.010 --> 06:27.887
There were two that weren't that bad.

06:36.896 --> 06:39.857
We will now take all candidates
for a medical check-up.

06:39.941 --> 06:42.360
You will be transported in pairs
by helicopter.

06:43.444 --> 06:44.862
- Mr. Taro!
- Hmm?

06:44.946 --> 06:46.197
Akira...

06:46.280 --> 06:47.990
I wanted to say thank you.

06:48.491 --> 06:50.451
If it weren't for you, Mr. Taro,

06:50.535 --> 06:52.787
I'm sure I wouldn't have passed this exam.

06:52.870 --> 06:56.374
When I see you at school,
please tell me more about Rion, okay?

06:56.457 --> 06:57.291
Sure.

06:57.834 --> 07:00.628
I'm so excited to go to school
with all of you!

07:00.711 --> 07:01.712
Me, too!

07:01.796 --> 07:03.089
- Yeah.
- Same.

07:03.172 --> 07:05.508
Mafuyu, are you alright?

07:06.008 --> 07:08.010
I know Shinaya got you pretty bad.

07:08.094 --> 07:09.095
Yeah.

07:09.178 --> 07:10.847
I'm fine.

07:12.473 --> 07:15.351
Ms. Toramaru and Mr. Seba
to this helicopter, please.

07:15.435 --> 07:17.019
See you, Shin.

07:19.897 --> 07:23.234
I don't get it. That was surprisingly dry.

07:23.317 --> 07:25.736
<i>- I expected something like this...</i>
- Come on now, please?

07:35.538 --> 07:37.039
Hurry up, get in.

07:40.376 --> 07:43.379
Bye, guys! See you!

07:48.176 --> 07:50.553
You good? You look really pale.

07:50.636 --> 07:51.679
I guess.

07:51.762 --> 07:53.931
Why'd I get paired with you, anyway?

07:54.015 --> 07:54.891
Don't ask me.

07:55.433 --> 07:56.851
Maybe we live in the same area?

07:57.351 --> 07:59.228
A boy and a girl, back from battle.

08:00.229 --> 08:02.690
A limitless blue sky ahead of them.

08:02.773 --> 08:07.528
The two ponder about the awaiting journey.
Their hearts filled with hope...

08:07.612 --> 08:11.032
Nevertheless! It is in moments like this

08:11.115 --> 08:14.035
that despair strikes again!

08:14.994 --> 08:15.870
You...

08:15.953 --> 08:17.997
What? Who is this guy?

08:18.080 --> 08:18.998
We need to get off!

08:19.081 --> 08:19.916
What?

08:22.460 --> 08:24.712
You don't get to call the shots, brat.

08:25.338 --> 08:27.048
Did you think life would be sweet?

08:27.131 --> 08:29.258
<i>That's enough, Carolina Reaper.</i>

08:32.762 --> 08:33.888
That was hot.

08:33.971 --> 08:36.182
<i>Please handle them with care.</i>

08:37.141 --> 08:39.227
Now that they are joining us,

08:39.769 --> 08:42.522
<i>they are our precious friends.</i>

08:51.239 --> 08:54.075
I'm exhausted.
This is toxic work culture, for sure.

08:54.158 --> 08:56.494
Are we not taking on most of the workload?

08:56.577 --> 08:58.788
What is that halfwit Kanaguri doing?

08:58.871 --> 09:01.082
Shooting a movie somewhere, I guess?

09:01.165 --> 09:02.208
So he's skiving off.

09:02.875 --> 09:05.628
Mr. Shishiba, let's fire him.

09:05.711 --> 09:07.380
I wish we could.

09:07.463 --> 09:10.341
It's beyond me why management
hired him in the first place.

09:10.424 --> 09:14.303
I heard that he had a huge fight
about a movie with an Order member

09:14.387 --> 09:15.721
and ended up killing them.

09:15.805 --> 09:17.223
So, Kanaguri took the spot.

09:17.932 --> 09:19.934
Talk about a broken system.

09:20.434 --> 09:22.311
LOTTERY TICKETS

09:23.813 --> 09:26.691
Hello, there.
Three Killer Lotto Scratch cards, please.

09:26.774 --> 09:28.609
Sure. That'll be 900 yen.

09:31.612 --> 09:34.407
Here you go. Split it even
if anyone wins 100 million.

09:34.991 --> 09:37.118
Stop saying that joke every time.

09:37.702 --> 09:39.704
We know there's no prize anyway.

09:40.204 --> 09:42.498
Mr. Shishiba, can I borrow a lucky coin?

09:42.582 --> 09:43.916
Just use your fingernail.

09:45.835 --> 09:47.211
You're no fun.

09:47.878 --> 09:48.838
Let's see.

09:49.338 --> 09:52.300
Hitman murdered in Kyoto.

09:52.383 --> 09:54.594
"X left at the scene."

09:54.677 --> 09:56.762
"Attack may be by Slur's group."

09:56.846 --> 09:58.014
"Go investigate."

09:58.097 --> 09:59.515
Same here.

09:59.599 --> 10:01.851
Another Slur-related case?

10:01.934 --> 10:04.812
And right in my own hometown,
for pity's sake.

10:05.313 --> 10:07.940
Is he seriously trying
to take down the JAA?

10:08.482 --> 10:10.860
What happens if the JAA gets destroyed?

10:11.569 --> 10:12.445
Will I be unemployed?

10:13.070 --> 10:14.614
That's your concern?

10:15.156 --> 10:18.576
If the JAA gets destroyed,
Japan would also be destroyed.

10:18.659 --> 10:21.996
Cities will overflow with criminals.

10:22.079 --> 10:23.331
But what about the police?

10:23.914 --> 10:28.586
The Japanese police's clearance rate
is maybe 30 percent at best.

10:28.669 --> 10:33.132
And that's the rate based on cases
that the police are aware of.

10:33.215 --> 10:35.593
I bet the true rate
is less than ten percent.

10:36.385 --> 10:41.098
Does that mean the remaining
90 percent of criminals are killed by us?

10:41.182 --> 10:43.893
Right. Well, it's not only criminals
that we kill.

10:43.976 --> 10:45.645
We take hit requests of any kind.

10:46.187 --> 10:49.649
So, that means,
I'm a hero fighting for justice...

10:50.191 --> 10:51.692
I wouldn't say that.

10:51.776 --> 10:52.610
Why not?

10:52.693 --> 10:54.945
There's no justice or villainy in murder.

10:55.446 --> 10:58.074
Although, in my opinion,

10:58.658 --> 11:03.079
an excessive sense of justice
can do much more harm than villainy.

11:06.207 --> 11:07.166
I won a prize.

11:07.667 --> 11:08.793
What?

11:08.876 --> 11:10.294
Didn't know you could actually win.

11:10.378 --> 11:12.338
Thought it was only for assignments.

11:12.421 --> 11:14.632
See, what'd I tell you?

11:14.715 --> 11:15.549
How much is it?

11:16.092 --> 11:17.093
20,000 yen.

11:17.176 --> 11:18.761
Treat us to lunch!

11:18.844 --> 11:21.597
No, it's all mine. I bought it.

11:21.680 --> 11:23.808
I literally saw Nagumo buy it.

11:25.768 --> 11:29.563
After intense battles,
the protagonist completes his exams.

11:30.689 --> 11:33.651
But, alas! He has been abducted!

11:34.235 --> 11:37.655
In this desperate situation,
what runs through the boy's mind?

11:37.738 --> 11:38.572
Drop dead.

11:38.656 --> 11:39.782
Cut.

11:40.491 --> 11:41.575
Too bland.

11:42.368 --> 11:43.494
Let's try again.

11:43.577 --> 11:45.871
Take 39, rolling!

11:45.955 --> 11:48.040
Do you mind, Kanaguri?

11:49.792 --> 11:53.212
Kanaguri, you are not at the JAA.

11:53.295 --> 11:55.798
Please stop acting on your own.

11:55.881 --> 11:56.715
CAROLINA REAPER

11:56.799 --> 11:59.135
How many shots do you want, idiot?

11:59.635 --> 12:02.805
Please be quiet.
I don't want background noise in my shot.

12:06.308 --> 12:11.021
Why do we have to wait around for you
and your good-for-nothing hobby?

12:11.105 --> 12:16.277
Time spent on movies is far more valuable
than your good-for-nothing life.

12:16.360 --> 12:18.696
Don't fight, big brother.

12:18.779 --> 12:19.613
CLUB JAM

12:20.197 --> 12:22.116
Please, hit me instead.

12:22.199 --> 12:23.826
We can have everyone watch

12:23.909 --> 12:26.829
as I bear terrible torture,
and Mr. Kanaguri can film it.

12:27.371 --> 12:28.998
That'll make everyone happy. See?

12:29.582 --> 12:31.709
I will not film something so distasteful.

12:31.792 --> 12:35.254
You're just saying that
because you want to be tortured!

12:35.337 --> 12:38.340
As punishment, hold your breath
until I give you permission.

12:39.925 --> 12:44.221
My goodness. I can't believe
how undisciplined you all are.

12:44.889 --> 12:46.599
<i>What the hell is wrong with them?</i>

12:47.349 --> 12:49.351
Toramaru, Mafuyu,

12:50.478 --> 12:53.397
you must be so confused,
being brought here all of a sudden.

12:54.023 --> 12:57.401
I want you to know that
we have no intention of harming you.

12:57.485 --> 13:00.362
After dragging us here like this?
Yeah, right.

13:00.863 --> 13:04.658
We are an organization
gathered for a single purpose.

13:05.159 --> 13:07.036
We are currently trying to expand,

13:07.119 --> 13:10.498
and we're recruiting young,
talented hitmen to join our cause,

13:10.581 --> 13:13.918
which is why we've invited you here.

13:14.627 --> 13:16.378
A single "purpose"?

13:16.462 --> 13:18.672
We want to destroy the JAA.

13:20.174 --> 13:21.175
Why?

13:22.259 --> 13:23.260
Why?

13:24.094 --> 13:25.429
Simply put,

13:25.930 --> 13:30.184
we want to restore
the natural way of the world...

13:31.227 --> 13:33.145
for noble justice.

13:37.024 --> 13:39.777
In case you're wondering,
we provide health insurance...

13:39.860 --> 13:40.861
OUR BENEFITS

13:40.945 --> 13:44.698
...guaranteed five to six-day work weeks,
no overtime, and lifelong employment.

13:47.743 --> 13:49.245
And what if I say no?

13:49.787 --> 13:51.288
If you say no...

13:58.504 --> 14:02.550
Oh... You can breathe now, Club Jam.

14:03.050 --> 14:03.968
SAKAMOTO'S

14:04.051 --> 14:05.970
Well, anyways...

14:06.053 --> 14:08.847
I didn't imagine the exam
would be so tough.

14:08.931 --> 14:11.767
You're amazing!
I knew you two could do it!

14:11.850 --> 14:14.937
I didn't expect
we'd be messing with Slur, though.

14:15.020 --> 14:17.314
I let my guard down
since it was just an exam.

14:17.815 --> 14:19.233
I'm jealous of you.

14:19.316 --> 14:23.237
JCC has a lot of awesome events.
You're gonna love it!

14:23.988 --> 14:26.991
You do realize
we're not going for fun, right?

14:27.074 --> 14:29.159
Our focus is on the JCC Databank.

14:29.243 --> 14:30.119
EXAM - INFILTRATE

14:30.202 --> 14:31.036
ACCESS DATABANK

14:31.120 --> 14:33.122
We're going in to get information on Slur.

14:33.205 --> 14:34.039
GET INTEL ON SLUR

14:34.123 --> 14:37.543
But you might as well
make some friends while you're there.

14:37.626 --> 14:40.462
Oh, that reminds me.
There was this one kid at the exam--

14:40.546 --> 14:42.298
Shin! Daddy!

14:43.132 --> 14:46.886
You got letters! It says it's from JCC!

14:49.221 --> 14:50.139
What's this?

14:50.222 --> 14:53.225
Oh, the exam results...

14:53.309 --> 14:54.143
- What?
- Huh?

14:56.478 --> 14:59.315
You got the top score! That's amazing!

14:59.398 --> 15:01.817
This exam is supposed to be super hard!

15:01.901 --> 15:04.111
I didn't know you had it in you!

15:04.194 --> 15:05.905
Good job, Shin!

15:05.988 --> 15:07.197
Good job!

15:07.281 --> 15:10.034
<i>I suppose I am getting a bit better.</i>

15:10.117 --> 15:10.951
THRILLED

15:11.035 --> 15:11.994
Wait a second.

15:12.578 --> 15:14.246
If Shin got the best score,

15:14.788 --> 15:16.123
what about Mr. Manager?

15:19.919 --> 15:20.753
I failed.

15:21.253 --> 15:22.087
What?

15:22.755 --> 15:24.924
What?

15:25.007 --> 15:28.093
Taro, did you forget to write
your name on an answer sheet?

15:28.177 --> 15:30.638
<i>I guess even monkeys fall from trees.</i>

15:30.721 --> 15:32.848
Poor Daddy.

15:32.932 --> 15:35.893
Maybe you've been eating
a little too much recently.

15:37.811 --> 15:40.981
There's no way Mr. Sakamoto failed.
It must be a clerical error!

15:41.065 --> 15:42.775
I'll give 'em a piece of my mind!

15:42.858 --> 15:44.234
I think he's overreacting.

15:44.318 --> 15:46.987
We couldn't let him pass. Sorry.

15:47.071 --> 15:48.197
What do you mean?

15:48.280 --> 15:49.907
You already told us he passed!

15:49.990 --> 15:51.742
<i>I kinda got carried away then.</i>

15:51.825 --> 15:53.118
<i>- To be honest...</i>
- Huh?

15:53.202 --> 15:56.664
I realized there's this section
in the JCC rules.

15:56.747 --> 16:00.584
"Persons with a bounty on their head
cannot be admitted."

16:02.086 --> 16:04.213
He's not making any sense.

16:04.296 --> 16:06.173
I'm gonna go talk to him in person.

16:06.256 --> 16:08.634
Yikes, he's an "ask for the manager" type.

16:08.717 --> 16:11.178
No need to worry. I have a good idea!

16:11.929 --> 16:14.056
Nagumo! How long have you been there?

16:14.556 --> 16:17.893
I heard you reapplied
for the JCC exam, Sakamoto.

16:17.977 --> 16:18.936
You really are a mor...

16:19.687 --> 16:21.855
an interesting person, Sakamoto!

16:22.856 --> 16:25.234
He almost called me a moron, didn't he?

16:25.317 --> 16:26.986
And you failed to boot!

16:28.028 --> 16:30.114
Wait, no! Calm down. Please!

16:30.197 --> 16:31.115
Mr. Sakamoto...

16:31.198 --> 16:33.951
Hey! What's that good idea
you were talking about?

16:34.034 --> 16:35.327
It's simple.

16:36.120 --> 16:39.123
If you can't get in as a student,
you can go as a teacher.

16:39.206 --> 16:40.207
Huh?

16:40.290 --> 16:41.875
"Student teacher"?

16:42.501 --> 16:45.295
The thing is, I was also trying
to get into the JCC,

16:45.379 --> 16:47.214
and I'd already started preparations,

16:48.298 --> 16:51.135
<i>but it conflicted with my trip to Kyoto
with my friends.</i>

16:51.635 --> 16:53.637
I was looking for someone to take my spot.

16:54.138 --> 16:56.807
<i>This actually is a good idea.</i>

16:56.890 --> 16:58.350
<i>I'll look for clues as a student,</i>

16:58.434 --> 17:00.644
<i>while Mr. Sakamoto investigates
as a teacher.</i>

17:01.145 --> 17:01.979
<i>But...</i>

17:02.062 --> 17:06.692
The issue that started this all
is that I can't step foot on JCC grounds,

17:06.775 --> 17:07.609
you moron.

17:07.693 --> 17:10.988
That's not a problem.
It just has to be someone else, right?

17:16.201 --> 17:17.369
What?

17:17.453 --> 17:18.620
Me?

17:20.414 --> 17:23.459
<i>This is Japan Clear Creation,
a training institute for hitmen,</i>

17:23.542 --> 17:28.297
<i>commonly known as the JCC.</i>

17:28.380 --> 17:31.383
<i>Approximately 1,000 students attend</i>

17:31.467 --> 17:34.053
<i>this four-year boarding school.</i>

17:34.136 --> 17:38.390
<i>Training courses are ruthless,
often resulting in the death of students.</i>

17:38.891 --> 17:41.310
<i>At the same time,</i>

17:41.393 --> 17:44.563
<i>those who excel may even
earn their license as a student.</i>

17:45.147 --> 17:47.024
<i>In other words...</i>

17:47.107 --> 17:52.780
<i>This is the most elite assassin
training institution in the country.</i>

17:53.280 --> 17:56.617
<i>Oh no... This place is so big,
I'm completely lost.</i>

17:56.700 --> 17:58.035
Hey, get outta the way!

17:58.118 --> 17:59.953
We're almost at the infirmary!

18:00.037 --> 18:01.830
Stay with us, alright?

18:01.914 --> 18:04.958
Another injury in Assassination Training?

18:05.042 --> 18:06.794
That's the tenth one this month.

18:07.419 --> 18:09.088
That wound looked gnarly.

18:09.171 --> 18:11.507
Without real skills,
you'd die pretty easily.

18:11.590 --> 18:12.424
<i>Oh my god...</i>

18:13.092 --> 18:16.929
During a mission,
you will always be watched by enemies,

18:17.012 --> 18:19.264
and you will always be in a time crunch.

18:19.348 --> 18:22.810
Therefore, we aim for critical hits
with minimal movement,

18:22.893 --> 18:25.020
and avoid leaving an unnecessary mess.

18:25.104 --> 18:27.147
This is the basic approach for any case.

18:27.231 --> 18:29.024
<i>Made it in the nick of time...</i>

18:29.108 --> 18:32.069
Let's try some one-on-one practice now.

18:32.152 --> 18:35.030
Can I have number 13, Mr. Tanishi,

18:36.448 --> 18:39.118
and the student in the back
who just came in.

18:39.618 --> 18:42.746
This is not Sneaking Practice.

18:44.081 --> 18:44.957
<i>I'm going to die...</i>

18:45.624 --> 18:46.708
Let's begin.

18:46.792 --> 18:49.753
We'll start with the basic moves
in close-quarters combat.

18:49.837 --> 18:53.090
Parry the attack by
redirecting the force of their strike.

18:53.590 --> 18:55.050
Let's start slow, okay?

18:55.134 --> 18:56.343
<i>He's huge.</i>

18:56.885 --> 18:58.303
<i>I'm fighting this shrimp?</i>

18:58.387 --> 18:59.680
ASSASSINATION MAJOR
JUMBO TANISHI

18:59.763 --> 19:00.764
<i>C'mon.</i>

19:00.848 --> 19:03.308
Don't lose to her, Tanishi!

19:04.143 --> 19:06.937
You will take turns, offense and defense.

19:07.479 --> 19:10.816
The knife is very real, so be careful.
Slowly, understood?

19:10.899 --> 19:13.569
<i>How 'bout a little jump scare?</i>

19:13.652 --> 19:16.780
Here I come, nice and slow.

19:18.198 --> 19:21.743
Hey! I told you not to--

19:22.369 --> 19:23.203
What?

19:33.213 --> 19:34.590
<i>Those moves...</i>

19:35.716 --> 19:37.718
I forgot to mention that

19:37.801 --> 19:41.555
we'll be having a student teacher
helping us out.

19:42.139 --> 19:43.765
How's that look?

19:43.849 --> 19:47.311
- What the... Whoa!
- Mr. Sakamoto, you're...

19:48.187 --> 19:49.897
That's amazing!

19:49.980 --> 19:52.399
You're a totally different person, honey!

19:52.482 --> 19:55.319
Turn me back this instant, Nagumo...

19:55.402 --> 19:57.946
Oh! Time for me to go.

19:58.488 --> 20:01.158
By the way, that disguise
will only last for 24 hours.

20:01.742 --> 20:03.827
You'd better find the databank by then.

20:04.494 --> 20:06.038
Good luck!

20:10.000 --> 20:12.211
<i>You'll pay for this, Nagumo!</i>

20:16.673 --> 20:19.176
I wonder how it's going with Sakamoto.

20:19.259 --> 20:22.012
Mr. Saka? What's he been up to?

20:22.095 --> 20:24.014
He's a beautiful student teacher now.

20:24.097 --> 20:24.932
Huh?

20:25.432 --> 20:28.310
Where'd you go, Natsuki? Hiding in here?

20:28.852 --> 20:30.312
I know you're here!

20:32.231 --> 20:33.857
What? Who are you?

20:34.441 --> 20:35.275
You new here?

20:36.109 --> 20:37.945
Of course! This must be...

20:39.404 --> 20:40.572
a core school experience

20:40.656 --> 20:43.158
"getting beat up by an upperclassman!"

20:44.117 --> 20:45.535
In case you're interested,

20:45.619 --> 20:49.373
I was trying out this one,
"cut class and smoke in the restroom".

20:49.456 --> 20:51.792
It was a little dream of mine, y'know?

20:51.875 --> 20:54.503
You think you're funny?
I'll kill you, you little--

20:57.965 --> 21:01.593
I guess that counts
as "please spare me, senpai!"

21:02.719 --> 21:06.556
Now, it's time I find information on Slur!

22:52.287 --> 22:54.998
<i>It seems like you need some guidance.</i>

22:55.582 --> 22:57.250
Don't go overboard.

22:57.334 --> 23:01.254
No worries.
My hitman license rank is "excellent"!

23:03.423 --> 23:05.759
<i>No matter how dangerous this might be,</i>

23:05.842 --> 23:09.054
<i>I don't want to let people
that are precious to me die.</i>

23:10.097 --> 23:11.973
<i>That's why I came here!</i>

23:17.854 --> 23:21.858
<i>Now, time to erase some memories.</i>

23:23.860 --> 23:25.862
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
